# Files the website does not use; kept out of the Vercel deployment to keep it small.
# The site needs: site/ (pages, assets, data, img/) and the catalogue PDFs it links to
# (since 21 Oct 2026 also Fluid_Handling_Catalogue_spread.pdf and FUEL.pdf, whose products are live).
# No "!" re-include rules: Vercel did not apply "!/output_v2/images/" after "/output_v2/*", so every
# product picture was left out of the deployment (404). List what to leave out instead
# (site/tests/deploy.test.mjs checks this).
/output/
/output_v2/batches/
/output_v2/reports/
/output_v2/extracted_products.json
/output_v2/extracted_products.manifest.json
/output_v2/review.html
/output_pilot_handtool/
/Fluid_Handling_mini_min_2.pdf
/Hand_Tool_Catalogue_low_res_with_cover.pdf
/Workshop_mini-compress.pdf
/backend/
/tests/
/site/tests/
/tools/
/review/
/venv/
/.venv/
*.py
/verify/
# Flipbook pages: the site loads the WebP copies (tools/build_flipbook_webp.py), not the PNG renders.
/site/assets/flipbook/*/page-*.png
# The extracted pictures (PNG) are the dataset's evidence: the site shows their clear WebP copies in
# site/img/ (tools/build_display_images.py). Not used by the website either: the unchecked lubrication
# scrape (Oct 2026) that was taken off the site (lubrication products now come from batch_3_fluid).
/output_v2/images/
/output_v2/lubrication_products.json
/output_v2/lubrication_products.csv
# The local preview of batches not approved yet is never deployed (output_preview_fluid/ holds the
# batch_3_fluid preview as it was approved on 21 Oct 2026).
/site/data/catalogue.preview.json
/output_preview_fluid/
